From 5ddd503c971e9f3ee04a5c9c4ce36a1b434a2d78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Gre=C5=84?= <witold.gren@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:20:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] rtsp: never let a dead client keep a battery camera awake

A stream task holds a use permit while it forwards frames, so anything
that stalls it keeps the camera connected. Seen on a Reolink Go Plus: the
camera stayed online for 30 minutes after a live view ended.

- send_to_appsrc: allocate a buffer per frame instead of the 32-buffer
  pool whose acquire_buffer(None) blocked forever once a stalled pipeline
  stopped releasing buffers (upstream #340)
- a flushing or not-playing appsrc ends the stream after 15 s instead of
  silently skipping frames forever
- the camera stream task gives up when its consumer has not taken a
  frame for 15 s

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/common/instance/gst.rs |  9 ++++-
 src/rtsp/factory.rs        | 78 ++++++++++++++++++++------------------
 2 files changed, 50 insertions(+), 37 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/common/instance/gst.rs b/src/common/instance/gst.rs
